Actually, "threaten" appears in the rogue-like game Omega (which I haven't
attempted in years).  I think it was an option in a "chat" menu with
a few different options.  Your success with it depended on the monster's
level, and whatever you happened to be wielding at the time.

If you did successfully threaten the critter, you were then given
another list of options to choose from.  If I recall correctly:
a) release them      (Very lawful -- they become peaceful then)
b) demand payment    (an object or cash, whatever they throw at you)
c) kill them anyway  (very Chaotic.  And you still got the kill XP!)

IMHO, however, we've got plenty of ammunition for alignment games,
so I see no real need to throw this stuff into Nethack (esp. if it
would annoy the Omega coders).  Though it Would be nice to at least
see what all these other monsters are carrying....

